<h2 id="how-to-choose">How to choose in six questions</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Is it cleared for your region and your exact use?</strong> FDA, CE/UKCA, Health Canada and TGA clear specific indications. A vendor with many clearances may not have one for the finding you need.</li>
<li><strong>Has it been tested on patients like yours?</strong> Ask for local validation or a pilot on your own studies before committing.</li>
<li><strong>How many false alerts will you handle?</strong> A tool that over-flags adds work instead of removing it. Ask for sensitivity and false-positive rates in a setting like yours.</li>
<li><strong>Does it fit your PACS and RIS?</strong> Results should appear in your normal worklist, not a separate screen.</li>
<li><strong>Where do images and reports go?</strong> Ask about hosting, de-identification and your local privacy rules (HIPAA, UK GDPR, PHIPA, the Australian Privacy Act).</li>
<li><strong>Who is responsible?</strong> The AI assists. The radiologist signs the report and stays accountable for it.</li>
</ol>

<div class="callout"><b>Note:</b> a regulatory clearance shows a tool met a safety and effectiveness standard for a stated use. It does not show the tool will improve your results or save your department time.</div>

